        <ArticleTitle>[Blood plasma kallikrein-kinin system in acute intestinal obstruction with the experimental use of hyperbaric oxygenation].</ArticleTitle>
        <Pagination>
          <MedlinePgn>39-43</MedlinePgn>
        </Pagination>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText>The model of acute mechanical ileus was created in 130 albino rats. Components of the blood kinin system were investigated. During the second day the kinin system of blood was activated, during the third day it was depleted. The use of one performance of HBO on the 2nd and 3d day of ileus decreased the level of kinin-forming factors. The investigations performed create prerequisites for using HBO and antikinin drugs in the postoperative period of acute ileus, control of the kinin system parameters being strictly observed.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
